Call site of retry.Do with a local closure returning ErrBusy or errDryRun: closure + Is/As guards + double %w.
Expect errDryRun bare (non-transient: returned as is), ErrGaveUp and ErrBusy behind "%w after %d attempts: %w",
ctx.Err() origins behind "retry: interrupted: %w". ErrBusy must NOT appear bare; errDryRun should not appear behind
the gave-up wrap (last only ever holds transient errors); no errors of other callers' closures.
-- args --
-fanout=1 cmd/cli/main.go:@retry_busy_call
